      "type": "THESIS",
      "tickers": [
        "FISV"
      ],
      "headline": "FISV: INITIATING LONG THROUGH A COVERED CALL; SHARES AT $54.69, $55 CALL SOLD FOR $8.62",
      "body": [
        "Fiserv has lost more than three-quarters of its value since its 2025 peak. I think the fall has gone too far.",
        "The old management pushed margins up by overcharging merchants, and clients left. Mike Lyons has since reset the forecasts and reversed the pricing, and Takis Georgakopoulos, who ran payments at JPMorgan, runs the merchant business.",
        "I am not yet sure enough of the turnaround to own the shares outright. So I bought them and sold the $55 call expiring 15 January 2027 for $8.62. The premium is 15.8% of what I paid. It is my income while I wait, and it lowers my break-even to $46.07. In return I give up any gain above $55.",
        "The position should also not move with the AI trade."
      ],
